message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "The Adversarial Reasoning Method: A Conceptual Framework Proposal Emphasizing Reflection and Long-Term Pattern Integration for Structured Clinical Diagnostic Reasoning"
authors:
  - family-names: West
    given-names: Claudia
    email: westcw01@gmail.com
version: "1.7"
date-released: 2026-09-01
url: "https://github.com/claudia-west/adversarial-reasoning-method"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
abstract: >
  ARM is a conceptual, eight-step framework proposal for structured clinical diagnostic reasoning (Observe, Represent, Compete, Attack, Challenge, Update, Reflect, Integrate). It has not been empirically validated. The manuscript proposes a case-series feasibility pilot as a precursor to simulation-based and randomized evaluation.
keywords:
  - "clinical reasoning"
  - "diagnostic reasoning"
  - "diagnostic error"
  - "medical education"
